WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.290
In the Cloning and Assembly Entry, select
SEAL Demo Plasmid.

2
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:11.200
This is a synthetic circular DNA example
with seven hundred sixty-two bases.

3
00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:14.090
Click Map to display its circular map.

4
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:18.890
The colored regions represent annotations,
and the enzyme labels mark predicted

5
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:23.600
restriction cuts. Click the AluI site at
position one hundred forty-six

6
00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:28.420
to inspect its location. Then open the
block's Actions menu and choose

7
00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:33.580
Restriction digest. Choose Cutters to focus
the list on enzymes with sites

8
00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:39.210
in this sequence. Select AluI and read the
preview before creating anything.

9
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:43.620
For this full circular block, the summary
reports two cuts and two

10
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:48.430
linear fragments. Their lengths are seven
hundred forty-two and twenty

11
00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.690
bases, which add back to the original
length.

12
00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:56.420
Click Digest. SEAL creates a separate block
for each fragment and links

13
00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:58.100
the results to the source block.
